<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 23 0 R/E(Today we start a batch of elderberry syrup: dark berries simmered down and sweetened with honey, sealed now and opened in Week 2.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

164 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 23 0 R/E(A syrup is one of the oldest ways to turn strong medicine into something sweet and gentle, perfect for soothing coughs and sore throats.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

165 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 23 0 R/E(To use: children 1 teaspoon, adults 1 tablespoon, up to 3 times a day; more than that loosens the bowels.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

166 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 23 0 R/E(Shelf life: about 2 weeks from the day you make it, in the fridge.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

167 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 23 0 R/E(Why a syrup? Elderberry's medicine, its purple anthocyanins, dissolves well in hot water. Simmering draws it out and honey sweetens it, while gentle cooking breaks down the raw berry's harmful parts.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

168 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 23 0 R/E(STEP-BY-STEP)/Pg 13 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

169 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 23 0 R/E(Elderberry Syrup)/Pg 13 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

170 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 23 0 R/E(1. Put 1 cup dried elderberries and 4 cups water in a pot.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

171 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 23 0 R/E(2. With a grown-up, boil, then simmer until the liquid cooks down by half \(about 45 minutes\).)/Pg 13 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

172 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 23 0 R/E(3. Cool a little, then strain out the berries, pressing to squeeze out every drop.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

173 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 23 0 R/E(4. When the liquid is warm, not hot, stir in 1 cup honey.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[18]>>
endobj

174 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 23 0 R/E(5. Pour into a clean jar; label it with tape and a sharpie: today's date and the open date.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[19]>>
endobj

175 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 23 0 R/E(6. Store in the fridge; open in Week 2.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[20]>>
endobj

176 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 23 0 R/E(TEACHER NOTES)/Pg 13 0 R/K[21]>>
endobj

