<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 23 0 R/E(TODAY'S WORD: MENSTRUUM. The liquid, like water, alcohol, or honey, that pulls a plant's medicine out.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[22]>>
endobj

178 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 23 0 R/E(How woven)/Pg 13 0 R/K[23]>>
endobj

179 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 23 0 R/E(Science: water dissolves elderberry's purple anthocyanins, while gentle cooking breaks down the raw berry's harmful parts.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[24]>>
endobj

180 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 23 0 R/E(Math: simmer the berry liquid down by half, then stir in 1 cup of honey, half as much as the liquid left.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[25]>>
endobj

181 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 23 0 R/E(Safety: no honey for a baby under one year, and check with a provider before using elderberry with any medicine.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[26]>>
